  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Thursday...\n\nBrief ridging over the region will provide warm and dry conditions\nthrough the afternoon before a shortwave trough moves through.\nThis will begin to bring scattered showers to south central MT\nlate this evening, moving east through the overnight hours. Energy\nbeing advected into the region behind the main troughing is \nexpected to create scattered showers and thunderstorms late\nSaturday morning through the evening. Thunderstorms are expected\nto remain on the weak side with weak 0-6km shear at 10-20kts and\nMUCAPE at 500 J/kg or less. Confidence is high that ridging will\nreturn for Sunday through mid week. A disturbance moving across\nnorthern MT late Sunday into Monday will bring a weak front\nthrough, but no precipitation is expected with this and winds will\nbe the main concern (gusts 25-35 mph). Late Wednesday into \nThursday, ensembles are either trying to bring in a Pacific \nshortwave or bring up monsoonal moisture and energy from the \nsouthwest. Either way there is moderate confidence on some kind of\nunsettled pattern, but the type of set up is uncertain at this \ntime. \n\nHigh temperatures will be in the 60s Saturday, warming to the 70s\nand low 80s by Tuesday, nearing 90 by mid week. TS",
